course: dictionary
lesson: 7305
title: Pitifully: a word that makes you feel sorry
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «The bird in the bird-cage was sobbing pitifully.» A sobbing bird sounds sad and hurt, so pitifully means in a way that makes people feel pity, or sorry for someone.
explain: Pitifully is an adverb. It tells you how something happens, so it often sits next to a verb like sobbing or an adjective like small. Ask yourself: is the writer making me feel sorry, or just saying something is very disappointing?
explain: In everyday talk, pitifully can mean very or disappointingly. «Pitifully small» means far too small to be any use, and «pitifully few» means very few. Use the sentence around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: Pitifully is an adverb, so it describes how something happens or how much.
fact: «Pitifully» means in a way that makes people feel pity, or sorry for someone.
fact: «Pitifully» can also mean disappointingly or very, as in «pitifully small» and «pitifully few».
fact: In maths problems, «pitifully few» means very few, not that anyone feels sorry.
fact: To check your meaning, read the sentence with your word in place of pitifully and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Panels and windows smashed, and the bird sobbed pitifully.» What does pitifully show? | It means the bird sang loudly | *It makes you feel sorry for the bird | It means the bird was very happy | It means the cart was brand new
exercise: A pupil writes: «The puddle was pitifully small.» What does pitifully mean here? | Sorry for the puddle | Dark and cold | Wet and shiny | *Far too small, very small
exercise: The maths problem says: «There were pitifully few apples left.» What does pitifully few mean? | Green apples only | Lots and lots of apples | *Very few apples | Apples that someone felt sorry for
test: «The lost puppy cried pitifully in the rain.» What does pitifully tell you? | *It shows the puppy is sad, so you feel pity | It shows the puppy is very happy | It shows the puppy ran away | It shows the rain is cold
test: «Only pitifully few people came to the match.» What does this mean? | Many people came happily | The match was cancelled | *Very few people came | Everyone came early
exam: In «The bird sobbed pitifully», which meaning fits best? | Very quickly and loudly | *In a way that makes you feel pity | Happily and with a smile | Disappointingly small
